  "query_preview": "..\nIssued 212 PM CST Sat Nov 21 2026\n\nMonday through Saturday:\n\nCold advection on nwly winds will continue into Mon evening as\nanother shortwave trough tracks across the nrn Great Lakes on \nMon. Polar high pressure will then likely remain in the \nvicinity of srn WI for Tue-Wed. There is some uncertainty with \nthe evolution of an elongated n-s shortwave trough that crosses \nthe Rockies into the central USA for the first half of the week.\nThe extended models are now showing fairly good agreement of \nthe srn portion of the wave amplifying Tue nt-Wed over the \nlower MS River Valley, but also with an amplifying upper wave\nand closed upper low to the north over WI and surrounding areas\nfor Thanksgiving Day. At the surface, an inverted sfc trough\nwill extend from the Ohio River Valley into se WI. Widespread\nlight rain, and possibly light snow well inland from the lake, \nwould result. However, this is a new trend for the extended \nmodels and confidence remains low at this time. Only slight \nchance for rain and snow are forecast at this time. Shortwave \nridging and quiet wx would return for Fri-Sat. \n\nGehring",
